This directory contains hand-maintained data. It was unfortunately more straightforward to build this by hand rather
than writing a parser for it.

For how to UPDATE these files (people entering/leaving parliament, party changes, ministerial reshuffles) see
docs/data-updates.md at the root of this repository. This file only records where the data originally came from.

people.csv:
One row per person, keyed by "person count". The "aph id" field is the identifier assigned by the aph.gov.au website,
used for looking up members in the Hansard (it appears in the URL of the person's APH profile page).

representatives.csv and senators.csv:
One row per period of service (a "stint") in the House of Representatives and the Senate respectively, going back
to 1980. Originally compiled by hand from the 41st parliamentary handbook's historical tables and maintained by hand
since.

ministers.csv:
Contains the periods when particular people were ministers. The data was originally taken from the 41st parliamentary
handbook's ministries tables.

shadow-ministers.csv:
Contains the periods when particular people were part of the shadow ministry, going back to 20th March 1996.

postcodes.csv:
From the Australian Bureau of Statistics <http://www.abs.gov.au/>

patches:
Contains patches for the XML files of the Hansard to fix any errors by hand that are too painful or ugly to try to fix
automatically.
